{"capability_report":{"encoding":"verislop.formalizer-capability-gap/0.1","gaps":[{"attempted_representations":["Represent Event and Input as fixed records, nullable event and row values as Option Int, fill as String restricted by the specified domain guard, and results as a list of fixed Row records. Sorted unique group names, list_range bucket indices, event filters, and total folds can preserve all aggregation, ordering, multiplicity, and causal filling requirements, including propagation of zero sums. This represents returned values but provides no observation of the Python module or its effects.","Use a leading universal Input binder and compare solve(input) with an inline primitive aggregation expression under the specified validity guard. This supports executable value comparisons but cannot distinguish implementations with identical returned values and different external effects or imports.","Use the raw Lean proposal envelope to describe operational properties. No registered executable Python module, import, or effect observation is supplied, and opaque Lean acceptance is explicitly insufficient for the required TESTED assurance."],"feature":"Observations of Python module exports, execution effects, and imported facilities","obligation_ids":["O1","R1"],"reason":"The provided AST can specify a total pure aggregation function and its exact JSON-compatible result, but its formulas observe only typed values. They do not express that solution.py exports solve(data), that executing the generated Python implementation performs no external I/O or other externally observable effects, or that its required facilities are exclusively from the Python standard library. Those operational requirements cannot be replaced with output equality without removing frozen acceptance criteria."}],"obligation_ids":["D1","O1","O2","O3","O4","O5","O6","O7","I1","R1"]}}